WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.192
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:06.030
DINO CHIESA: Dino here.

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:07.980
In the previous
video in this series,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.770
we learned the basics
of the API portal.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:13.530
In this video, we will
learn how to publish APIs

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.410
to the portal to enable other
developers to find and use

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:17.820
them.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.820
Back to the Apigee
administrative UI.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:24.240
I can add APIs here.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:30.770
To add an API, we select from a
list of existing API products.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:34.360
We created an API product
in the previous video.

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.850
This is the thing that
external developers

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:41.960
subscribe to in order to
get keys to use the APIs.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:44.405
So I'll select that
previous API product.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.860
Now it's asking for a spec.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:52.910
This is an OpenAPI spec
document that describes

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:56.200
the API being published here.

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.770
The document includes
method and URL path pairs.

00:00:59.770 --> 00:01:01.540
This spec is the
thing that allows

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:06.480
you to generate interactive
documentation for the API.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.420
You can create that spec
using any tool or even

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.860
Apigee Edge itself.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:13.450
I'll upload my spec here.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:20.220
Back in the developer portal,
now we see the API product.

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:20.720
Great.

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.000
Clicking through, I can
see the API documentation.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:30.970
The spec we use defines
a very simple API

00:01:30.970 --> 00:01:38.200
with a single method/path
pair, get /, a very simple API.

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:43.100
Expanding that, I can
actually try the operation.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.420
Hmm, it's asking for an API key.

00:01:46.420 --> 00:01:48.970
As a developer, how
can I get one of those?

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:56.260
To get a key, a developer
needs to sign in.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:02:00.730
The portal implements a really
simple email-based sign-in.

00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:04.760
Users provide their
email address,

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.920
and then a click-through
on the verification

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:10.662
link in the email that gets
sent to them signs them in.

00:02:10.662 --> 00:02:11.495
There's no password.

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:19.060
As a developer, once signed
in, I can see my apps.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:24.430
I can see that I don't have
any, so let me create one.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:29.020
Name it, provide a description.

00:02:29.020 --> 00:02:33.640
Clicking through, I can manage
the products for that app.

00:02:33.640 --> 00:02:40.350
Let's turn on access for
that API product and save it,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.540
and then I can see my API key.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:49.800
Now let's try the interactive
documentation again.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:56.350
Paste in my API
key, and it works.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.270
Of course, your
API specifications

00:03:01.270 --> 00:03:03.590
will be more
complicated than this,

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:07.860
but the documentation will
render nicely for you.

00:03:07.860 --> 00:03:12.030
For example, here's what
the API for healthcare.gov

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.310
looks like in the
Apigee developer portal.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.300
The portal seems like
a simple website,

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.230
but it's more than that.

00:03:22.230 --> 00:03:25.400
This is the digital connection
between API consumer developers

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:29.870
and your APIs, a key
part of your API program.

00:03:29.870 --> 00:03:32.690
Remember, the Apigee
documentation and the community

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.750
are good resources
to learn more.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.880
Until next time,
keep it digital.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.230
[MUSIC PLAYING]

